    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Over the past several days, have you found yourself needing much less sleep than usual without feeling tired?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S036",
      "patient_response": "Well, you know, it's funny you ask that, because sleep has just been... it's been completely different lately. I mean, usually I'm the kind of guy who needs a solid seven or eight hours, especially with the physical work I do, lifting folks and being on my feet all day. But for the last, oh, maybe four or five days? It's like someone just flipped a switch in my head. \n\nI'll go to bed around, say, midnight, after tossing and turning and trying to wind down, and then boom—two, maybe three hours later, my eyes just snap open. And I don't mean waking up groggy and reaching for the snooze button. I mean wide awake, completely energized, like I just drank a pot of coffee. It'll be 3:00 AM, pitch black outside, the whole house is dead silent, and I'm just lying there thinking, \"Well, I'm up, let's get the day started!\" \n\nAnd I don't feel tired at all. That's the crazy part. I'll get out of bed, go into the kitchen, maybe start making a list of things I need to do at work, or reorganizing the pantry, or sketching out these ideas I have for better wheelchair ramps... just making all these plans while it's still dark out. And I honestly don't even think twice about it. It just feels perfectly normal to be up and running on two hours of sleep. I don't drag during the day, I don't need a nap... my motor just keeps running and running. So, yeah, I guess you could say I've been needing a whole lot less sleep.",
